/*
 * Utility-mount modules — chaff and heat-sink launchers, point defence, shield boosters, and the utility-slot scanners.
 *
 * The `utility` slice of Frontier's outfitting catalogue: each module's identity
 * AND its engineering/mechanical stats, joined on the Frontier `symbol`.
 *
 * Sources: EDCD FDevIDs, outfitting.csv (identity: symbol, category, name, class,
 *          rating, mount?, guidance?, ship?, entitlement?)
 *          https://github.com/EDCD/FDevIDs
 *          EDCD/coriolis-data, modules/** (stats: mass, power, performance, …)
 *          https://github.com/EDCD/coriolis-data
 *          The stat values are Elite Dangerous game data, property of Frontier
 *          Developments plc, redistributed under Frontier's media-usage terms:
 *          https://forums.frontier.co.uk/threads/510879/
 *
 * `symbol` is the internal identifier (e.g. `Hpt_PulseLaser_Fixed_Small`); `name`
 * the display name; `class` the module size (0-8) and `rating` its grade letter
 * (A-I) — the "5A" the outfitting screen shows. Identity fields always present;
 * every stat field is optional, present only where the module has it (masses in
 * tonnes, power in MW, jump ranges in LY). `restrictedToShips` lists the hull(s) a
 * non-armour module is limited to; armour's hull restriction is its `ship` field.
 *
 * Defence stats: `kineticResistance`, `thermalResistance`, `explosiveResistance` and
 * `causticResistance` are fractions of damage removed (negative = a weakness);
 * `hullBoost` is an armour variant's bonus as a fraction of the hull's base armour
 * (0.8 means base armour x 1.8), `hullReinforcement` is hull points added,
 * `shieldAddition` shield megajoules added, `moduleProtection` the fraction of module
 * damage absorbed. `alwaysPowered` marks a hardpoint-mounted module that draws its
 * power even with hardpoints retracted.
 * Weapon stats: `damage` is per round (per second on continuous-fire beam and mining
 * lasers, which carry no `rateOfFire`), `damageDistribution` splits it by type,
 * `rateOfFire` is shots per second with the burst pattern and charge time folded in,
 * `distributorDraw` (MW) and `thermalLoad` are per shot, and `maximumRange` /
 * `falloffRange` / `shotSpeed` are metres and metres per second.
 * `cost` is the standard purchase price in credits before any station discount;
 * it is omitted, never zeroed, where no registry publishes one (0 is a real price).
 *
 * Full provenance: data/ships/SOURCES.md.
 */
